# MoE OTD two-tier device-resident slot pool
#
# try_prepare_partial_upload (src/plugin/ops/moe_offload_constant.cpp:65,
# pre-patch) always called the two-arg allocate_memory(upload_layout, false),
# which resolves to get_lockable_preferred_memory_allocation_type
# (runtime/engine.cpp:110): supports_allocation returns false for usm_shared
# unconditionally (engine.cpp:97-101), so on every card this ran on the
# branch was not "shared, else host" - it was always usm_host, i.e. GTT, no
# matter how much VRAM was free. This patch charges each MoE expert slot
# buffer's bytes against a new per-compile device budget in program order
# (earlier MoE layers land in VRAM, the rest on the existing host path once
# the budget is spent - the granularity is forced by the data model: one
# constant is one memory object, so a tensor cannot be half device) and
# allocates usm_device while there is room. Applied against the pinned
# runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of patches/0003-0004.
#
# New plugin config property: MOE_OTD_DEVICE_POOL_BYTES
# (ov::intel_gpu::moe_otd_device_pool_bytes, size_t, RW). Device-resident
# budget in bytes for MoE OTD expert slot buffers under offload_ratio.
# Default 0 - every slot stays on the pre-existing usm_host path, i.e. no
# behaviour change until a caller sets it. Wired the same way offload_ratio
# is: options.inl (storage/getter), openvino/runtime/intel_gpu/properties.hpp
# (public Property<> declaration), plugin.cpp (supported RW property),
# compiled_model.cpp (RO on the compiled model). Deriving a value for it from
# a fit computation (arcint's `--expert-device-slots-mib auto`,
# docs/design-m9-offload-v2.md §3) is out of scope for this patch - out of
# scope for src/ this task at all.
#
# Allocation failure is a per-buffer fallback to the pre-existing usm_host
# path, counted in alloc_fallbacks (patches/0004), never fatal: an
# allocate_memory throw at compile time would otherwise kill the whole model
# load, which would make offload unusable on exactly the card M9's exit
# criterion names (16 GiB, where the pool does not fit uncapped).
#
# Lock-site audit (owed by docs/design-m9-offload-v2.md §1 before this patch,
# since a stray lock
# on a usm_device buffer does not throw - gpu_usm::lock, ocl_memory.cpp:521,
# allocates a host buffer sized to the *full* constant layout, because the
# slot memory is a reinterpret_buffer of a smaller physical allocation onto
# that full layout, and blocking-memcpys into it; today that is a cheap
# pointer return, under this patch it becomes a multi-GiB host allocation
# plus a device read past the actual allocation - silent, not a crash).
# Enumerated every mem_lock<>/.lock()/buffer_ptr() reachable from a data
# node's (constant's) attached memory, by grepping every file that touches
# data_node::get_attached_memory plus a plain mem_lock<> sweep of
# src/graph and src/plugin, then reading each site's call-context to check
# whether MoE routed-expert weight/scale/zp constants can reach it:
#
#   - src/plugin/ops/constant.cpp:132 (create_data). Already guarded by
#     `!partial_upload.enabled` before this patch (unrelated to it).
#   - src/graph/data.cpp:28-29 (attach_or_copy_data, called from every
#     data_inst ctor - the one production-reachable site). Short-circuits via
#     `mem->is_allocated_by(engine)` in the ordinary case (compile-time and
#     network-construction-time engine are the same instance), but nothing
#     proves that always holds (weight sharing / model-cache import across a
#     different engine context). This is the site the new otd_device_slot
#     guard (below) actually protects.
#   - src/graph/mutable_data.cpp:25-26 (same attach_or_copy_data pattern, for
#     mutable_data nodes). Unreachable: MoE routed-expert weights are `data`
#     nodes, never `mutable_data`.
#   - src/graph/graph_optimizer/prepare_primitive_fusing.cpp:392-407
#     (recalculate_biases). Gated to eltwise-Add constants shaped like a
#     per-channel conv/FC bias next to a fusable eltwise; MoE weight/scale/zp
#     constants feed MOECompressed's dedicated inputs directly, never a
#     generic bias-eltwise pattern. Unreachable.
#   - src/graph/graph_optimizer/pre_replace_deconv.cpp:220-290 (weight/bias
#     repack). Gated to Deconvolution inputs. Unreachable.
#   - src/graph/graph_optimizer/prepare_quantization.cpp:385-495 (threshold
#     merge). Gated to `quantize` (FakeQuantize) node dependencies 1-4.
#     Unreachable: MoE weight/scale/zp constants are never `quantize` inputs.
#   - src/graph/graph_optimizer/concat_input_order.cpp:69-70
#     (shuffle_weights). Gated to a `fully_connected` node's weight constant
#     feeding a Concat, dtype bitwidth >= 8. Unreachable: MoE weights feed
#     the fused moe_3gemm_fused_compressed primitive, never a plain
#     fully_connected node.
#   - src/graph/graph_optimizer/propagate_constants.cpp (const folding). No
#     mem_lock/.lock() call in the file at all - it does not lock memory to
#     do its job. Safe.
#   - src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/slice_scatter.cpp:42, src/graph/impls/ocl/
#     slice.cpp:20, src/graph/impls/ocl/non_max_suppression.cpp:170-185,
#     src/graph/loop.cpp:122/875/878/957/960, src/graph/impls/onednn/
#     utils.cpp:53-54/779, src/graph/primitive_inst.cpp:1377/1691,
#     src/graph/program_node.cpp:1333 (post-op-fusion inplace update, guarded
#     `!= usm_device` already, falls to a copy_to/copy_from round-trip on
#     usm_device instead of locking). All execution-time locks on inputs/
#     outputs of specific primitive types (Loop, NMS, Slice, SliceScatter,
#     zero-point conversion for an onednn conv, shape_info, a Gather index,
#     post-op-fusion scratch). None of these primitive types ever consumes a
#     MoE routed-expert weight/scale/zp constant - by construction the only
#     consumer is MOECompressed (moe_offload_constant.cpp's own role
#     classification). Unreachable.
#
# The guard: `memory::otd_device_slot` (include/intel_gpu/runtime/memory.hpp,
# next to the existing `from_memory_pool` flag, same pattern), set on the
# reinterpret_buffer result when try_prepare_partial_upload picks usm_device.
# gpu_usm::lock's usm_device branch now asserts !otd_device_slot before doing
# the bounce-copy. Deviation from the design's literal wording ("a debug-build
# guard"): implemented as an unconditional OPENVINO_ASSERT rather than one
# compiled only under a debug macro, matching the house convention already at
# the line this patch touches next to (moe_offload_constant.cpp:74's
# OPENVINO_ASSERT on the same code path) rather than introducing a second
# convention; the check is a single bool read, not a measurable cost, and a
# guard that silently compiles out in the release build customers actually
# run is the exact failure mode docs/design-m9-offload-v2.md §1's P1 bullet
# on lock() risk warns about.
#
# Fusion-impact obligation (0.3.0 ground rule 2, DESIGN §8): this patch
# changes the allocation *type* of constants feeding MOECompressed, which the
# ground rule flags as exactly the class of change that can flip a graph-
# optimiser decision about whether a node is treated as a lockable constant.
# DISCHARGED, not merely owed: DESIGN §7.0.2v records the compiled-graph
# check on real hardware under this patched plugin - the base model still
# fuses x40 (graph dump) - so the allocation-type change did not flip the
# fusion decision. That measurement was taken by the orchestrator's on-GPU
# pass, not by this task (no GPU device access, no compile_model, from this
# host); this patch itself was only built (CPU-only, ninja), never loaded.
diff --git a/src/plugins/intel_gpu/include/intel_gpu/runtime/memory.hpp b/src/plugins/intel_gpu/include/intel_gpu/runtime/memory.hpp
--- a/src/plugins/intel_gpu/include/intel_gpu/runtime/memory.hpp
+++ b/src/plugins/intel_gpu/include/intel_gpu/runtime/memory.hpp
@@ -136,6 +136,18 @@
     std::shared_ptr<MemoryTracker> get_mem_tracker() const { return m_mem_tracker; }
     bool from_memory_pool = false;
 
+    // arcint M9 (patches/0005, P1 two-tier device pool). Set on a constant's
+    // memory object when try_prepare_partial_upload (src/plugin/ops/
+    // moe_offload_constant.cpp) allocates it as usm_device: the slot buffer
+    // is a reinterpret_buffer of a smaller physical allocation onto the full
+    // constant layout, so gpu_usm::lock's device-USM branch would silently
+    // bounce-allocate a host copy sized to the full constant on any stray
+    // caller (a mem_lock<>, or attach_or_copy_data seeing a different engine
+    // at network-construction time) rather than throwing. This flag lets
+    // lock() fail loudly there instead; every non-OTD memory object leaves
+    // it false and pays nothing. See the lock-site audit in that patch.
+    bool otd_device_slot = false;
+
 protected:
     engine* _engine;
     const layout _layout;
